      "text": "CSE-198 - Directed Group Study Units: 2-4 Computer science and engineering topics whose study involves reading and discussion by a small group of students under supervision of a faculty member. Course Objectives: A Triton Enrollment Authorization (TEA) request is required for booking. It is the student's responsibility to find a CSE faculty sponsor to approve this request. A section ID will be added to the Triton Student System (TSS) for booking. Qualifications Computer Science and engineering topics whose study involves reading and discussion by a small group of students under the supervision of a faculty member. Prerequisites: Consent of instructor. Department approval required. Please see your CSE Degree Program website for unit limitations on special studies courses. Offered: Every quarter.",
